<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yusuf Lule</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–1985</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yusuf Lule was a Ugandan academic and politician who served as president of Uganda for 68 days in April–June 1979, after the overthrow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>. A former principal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makerere-university">Makerere University</a> College, he was chosen as leader of the Uganda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> at the Moshi conference of exiles but was removed by its council in June 1979. He later founded the Uganda Freedom Fighters, which joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s movement during the Bush War.</p></div>
